SAM Interface Support
Some Programing Language don't support Function Type. So they use a different Interface Method known as Single Abstract Method(SAM).
SAM Interface is an Interference with one abstract method. This is used in Java too.
JAVA Eg:
interface OnClick {
    void onClick(View view);
}
The communication between Java and Kotlin should be messy. But Kotlin coverts Lambda to SAM Interface.
But there is still a problem. Java needs a real interface to work with. Hence we create a Functional Interference to solve this.
Syntax:
fun interface OnClick { ... }
Android Listeners (Before Kotlin's Magic):
button.setOnClickListener(new View.OnClickListener() {
    @Override
    public void onClick(View v) {
        Toast.makeText(context, "Clicked!", Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show();
    }
});
Android Listeners (With Kotlin's SAM Support):
button.setOnClickListener {
    Toast.makeText(context, "Clicked!", Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show()
}
